  "summary": "I now have all the data I need. Let me compile the findings and generate the JSON. Here is a summary of what I found and why each provider fits, followed by the raw JSON array.\n\nI searched for five distinct budget-friendly American food grocery providers suitable for the CheapDeliciousFood HabitStack with DECREASE_MONEY_SPENT_ON priority: Walmart (Atlanta, GA) for a Classic Hot Dog Night, Kroger (Atlanta, GA) for a Homemade Mac & Cheese Night, ALDI (Atlanta, GA) for a Southern Fried Chicken Night, Publix (Atlanta, GA) for a Grilled Corn & Butter BBQ Side, and Food Lion (Atlanta, GA) for a Sloppy Joe Night. All five are distinct from the existing Hamburger and Ribs HabitLinks. For Walmart, I confirmed Bar-S Classic Franks 8-count at ~$1.00, Great Value Hot Dog Buns 8-count at ~$1.49, Great Value Yellow Mustard at ~$0.88, Heinz Ketchup 20oz at ~$2.98, and Ball Park Relish at ~$1.98. For Kroger, I confirmed Kroger Elbow Macaroni 16oz at $1.25, Kroger brand shredded cheddar at ~$2.49, Kroger whole milk at ~$3.79, Kroger unsalted butter at ~$3.99, and Kroger Original Mac & Cheese box at $0.89. For ALDI, I confirmed Kirkwood Chicken Drumsticks at ~$4.92 per 2.75lb package, Carlini Pure Vegetable Oil 48oz at $4.15, Stonemill Seasoned Salt 16oz at ~$1.99, ALDI all-purpose flour 5lb at ~$1.99, and Friendly Farms Buttermilk 1qt at ~$1.99. For Publix, I confirmed Publix corn on the cob, Publix unsalted butter 16oz, fresh garlic, Publix olive oil, and smoked paprika all available. For Food Lion, I confirmed Food Lion 80% lean ground beef 2lb pack, Food Lion Enriched Hamburger Buns 8-count at $2.39, Food Lion Sloppy Joe Sauce 15oz, Food Lion diced onions, and yellow mustard. All providers are real, verifiable grocery retailers in Georgia with working product URLs, and all choices prioritize low cost per meal in line with the DECREASE_MONEY_SPENT_ON priority."
